<ResourceDictionary xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
                    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml">

  <!--
    Sidebar rail glyphs. All geometries are authored against a 24x24 viewBox
    and rendered through a Path whose Fill binds to the host ToggleButton's
    Foreground, so the icon inverts to white when the nav entry is checked.
    EvenOdd (F0) fill is used wherever the silhouette has interior cut-outs
    (e.g. the doorway in the dungeon arch, the sprocket holes in the film
    strip) so a single sub-path list draws the framed shape.
  -->

  <!--
    M+ — arched dungeon gateway traced from `screenshots/icon/dungeon.png`
    with potrace (-t 25 to drop sub-pixel specks left over from the bilevel
    source) and renormalised into the standard 24x24 viewBox by the bake
    script. Voussoir blocks frame an arched door panel with iron-strap
    notches at top and bottom, side wall blocks, and floor stones. The path
    is self-intersecting; NonZero (default) is the correct fill rule —
    potrace draws hole sub-paths in the opposite direction so they cancel
    naturally without the EvenOdd prefix.
  -->
